//! Managed turn preparation and provider execution for the future mounted AgentLoop.
//!
//! The preparation path reuses the mounted provider-epoch binding, rerenders
//! only User after context replacement, and creates reducer/dispatcher state
//! only for the final Ready candidate. Provider execution is then spawned onto the owner
//! runtime so cancelling the caller only requests cancellation: the task still
//! joins the provider and explicitly aborts the attempt before it exits.
//!
//! [`MountedAgent`] owns the authoritative epoch/session/revision snapshot,
//! borrowed call props, per-candidate owned turn props, fork/reconfigure,
//! cancellation-safe provider cleanup, and receipt-gated durable writeback.
//! It remains internal while reducer/persistence configuration and the public
//! call builder are still being defined.

